 Justin Pearson of the 'Tennessee Three' won a crowded Democratic primary with strong name recognition.\n\nRatings across the board call the race a Republican flip, ranging from Likely to Safe R, and Polymarket prices Pearson's chances near 13%. A September Hart poll showed Taylor ahead 48-44. Pearson has raised more money and earned endorsements from Kamala Harris and National Nurses United, but the district's new lean and the consensus of outside assessments make Taylor the favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1065, "margin": -7.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.132, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1308, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -8.0}]}